From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:03:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 91/94] runtime: retain EE context transitions for manual crash
 diagnosis

Keep the last 32 scheduler transitions in fixed storage without normal-path I/O; dump them and live nested contexts on missing targets, guest exceptions and uncaught executor faults. Capture PC/RA/SP/EPC and delay-slot identity before invocation and scheduling changes. No guest behavior change or claim of fixing the skill-move fault.

PS2RuntimeKernel covers wraparound, nested saved contexts and reset. Verified rx build and rx test --full (57/57). One 60-second match probe reached play at 50.0 FPS without a fault; its audio check failed with 123 steady-state underruns.

